description: DISTILLATION STUDENT, SMALLER. Same recipe as v016 but 2x96 instead of
  2x128 -- 116,546 params against a 192,258-param teacher (0.61x).
hypothesis: 'Distillation regularises, and dozken''s own results show the effect clearly:
  from a 872k teacher, their 436k student scored 0.6879 and their SMALLER 314k student
  (0.36x) scored 0.6888 -- smaller beat larger on the public board, confirmed at 55m16s
  vs 61m06s. If that holds here, a student below the teacher should beat v016''s equal-size
  one, AND inference would drop to roughly 20 us/row.

  Expected: match or beat v016''s 0.679986-equivalent, and if it wins, cut inference
  cost by ~40%. If instead the smaller student is clearly worse, the regularisation
  story is size-sensitive and the sweet spot is near the teacher''s own width -- which
  is itself the useful answer, and matches v014 showing 379k is a dead heat with 192k.'
change_vs_parent: 'ONE change off gru_v016: model.hidden 128 -> 96 (192,258 -> 116,546
  params). Unchanged: distill_weight 0.5 and the same teacher labels, the soft mask,
  state_reset 4000 in training and inference, chunk_len 2000, aux weighted-MSE 0.05,
  EMA 0.999, seed 1337, 3-epoch cosine schedule.

  0.61x the teacher is deliberately between dozken''s winning 0.36x and their losing-on-size
  0.50x-equal student, chosen to answer the question without repeating their exact
  point on a different codebase.'
